%!PS-Adobe-3.0
%%Title: Paintkit -- a backdrop per band: pkwet /Box and /Bands (issue #359)
%%BoundingBox: 0 0 640 310
%%EndComments

% Specimen for pkwet's banded /Under (lib/paintkit.ps). pkwet grades each
% softening pass toward /Under, "the colour already on the canvas there".
% With a procedural /Under and /At (issue #179) that is one colour per pass,
% asked at the pass's displaced anchor, so a mark that is tall against the
% backdrop still has the rim its own height makes: the pass that is right at
% the anchor is wrong at the foot and the head.
%
%   /Box [x y w h]     where the mark sits, in the user space pkwet is called in
%   /Bands [cols rows] a grid over the box, grown by /Offset on every side
%   /Under { ... }     asked once per cell, at the cell's centre
%
% Each softening pass is then run once per cell, clipped to it, and mixed
% toward that cell's backdrop. The core is laid once, whole.
%
% Left: one tall plume over a strongly graded sky, /Under a procedure with
% /At at the plume's middle: the outer passes are a pale grey against the
% cold zenith and a cold blue against the warm horizon, a visible collar at
% both ends. Right: the same plume, same seed, same marks, /Box over it and 12
% rows: each band of every pass is mixed toward the sky at its own height
% and the collar is gone. Only the colours differ; the random stream is
% replayed per cell, so every cell lays the same marks and the clips cut
% them into pieces.
%
% A cell wants to be no taller than about half /Offset, and the mark runs
% (Layers - 1) x cells + 1 times, which has to stay within the 64 a chain of
% such calls is budgeted: 4 x 12 + 1 = 49 here. A mark about as tall as
% /Offset is as well served by /At, and cheaper.
%
%   pscat --page 640x310 examples/paintkit_wet_bands_demo.ps --png wet_bands.png

(lib/artkit.ps) run
(lib/paintkit.ps) run

/SKYTOP [0.06 0.16 0.50] def
/SKYLOW [0.98 0.86 0.68] def
/SKYH 230 def
/skyat {                                   % y -> r g b   (0 horizon .. SKYH zenith)
    SKYH div 0 max 1 min /skt exch def
    SKYLOW SKYTOP skt mix3
} def

1 1 1 setrgbcolor clippath fill

/label {                                   % x y string -
    gsave
        0.30 0.30 0.30 setrgbcolor
        /Helvetica findfont 9 scalefont setfont
        3 1 roll moveto show
    grestore
} def

% One 300 x 230 panel at (px, 50): the graded sky and the same tall plume,
% softened by pkwet with the /At form or the /Box form.
/panel {                                   % px banded? -
    /ppro exch def /ppx exch def
    gsave
        ppx 50 translate
        newpath 0 0 moveto 300 0 lineto 300 SKYH lineto 0 SKYH lineto closepath clip
        0 1 SKYH 1 sub {
            /pgy exch def
            pgy skyat setrgbcolor
            newpath 0 pgy moveto 300 pgy lineto 300 pgy 2 add lineto 0 pgy 2 add lineto
            closepath fill
        } for
        0.99 0.98 0.97 setrgbcolor
        41 srand
        {
            newpath 150 30 moveto 140 90 160 150 150 205 curveto
            << /Nozzle 13 /Density 380 /Falloff 1 /Speck 1.1 /Overspray 0.4 >> pkspray
        }
        ppro
            { << /Soft 1 /Offset 30 /Layers 5
                 /Box [ 110 30 80 175 ] /Bands [ 1 12 ] /Under { exch pop skyat } >> }
            { << /Soft 1 /Offset 30 /Layers 5
                 /At [ 150 118 ] /Under { exch pop skyat } >> }
        ifelse
        pkwet
    grestore
} def

0   false panel
340 true  panel

10  295 (/At [ 150 118 ]: one backdrop per pass) label
350 295 (/Box [ 110 30 80 175 ] /Bands [ 1 12 ]: one per band) label
10  36 (each pass is mixed toward the sky at the plume's middle: a pale collar) label
10  24 (round the top and a cold blue one round the warm foot) label
350 36 (each band of each pass is mixed toward the sky at its own height) label
350 24 (same seed, same marks, the collar is gone) label

showpage
